# Sphinx's Approach with only three copies in the graveyard: Emry mills three Sphinx's Approach and an Island, so the
# graveyard does not hold the four cards the action needs. The action is impossible, so no question is asked (the bare
# refusal, CR 608.2d), nothing is exiled and no search happens; the resolving spell itself reaches the graveyard only after
# the check, so it cannot be one of the four (CR 608.2c).

